# .rewrite-cache.json — SAME FILE, OPPOSITE NATURE IN THE TWO REPOS (2026-08-04).
#
# In the author's private repo it is now VERSIONED: with the Gemini call gone there is no
# generator left to rebuild it, so losing it would silently cost recall (measured there:
# 21/24 training and 14/14 held-out with it, 18/24 and 12/14 without).
#
# Here it stays IGNORED, and not by oversight. This cache fills up with identifiers mined from
# whatever codebases the machine points at — class and function names straight out of private
# repos. Versioning it here would turn a local optimisation into a leak channel that grows on
# its own, in a repo whose whole design rule is "carries nothing personal". Same file, same
# code, different repo, different answer.
.rewrite-cache.json
